new('être','être','noun masculine singular','being; an entity that exists',['a place','a time','a movement'],'Le terme général pour ce qui existe, quelle que soit sa nature, est un ___.',['être','endroit','moment','mouvement'],'Quel nom masculin désigne de manière générale une entité qui existe ?','prior:chapter-01-identity-plan.json:etres_beings',[(169,36)],'L’Être éternel refers to the divine being, a noun rather than copular or auxiliary être. The earlier Chapter I plural general-entities plan and singular living-being plan were inspected. Share the general-entities meaning and reconcile the narrower singular wording; its new-sense route must be corrected to a proper French noun lemma before import; the published être verb cannot own this noun. Add a deity-context bank on general being, without claiming a material living creature or copying verb mastery. Être/endroit/moment/mouvement are masculine singular, and the general existence clue selects être.')
new('être','être','verb infinitive absolute existence','exist; have existence',['become','remain in a place','disappear'],'Il vaudrait mieux ne pas exister : il vaudrait mieux ne pas ___.',['être','devenir','séjourner','disparaître'],'Quel infinitif employé absolument signifie exister ?','sns_fr_etre_existential',[(204,207)],'Autant vaudrait ne pas être means not existing, rather than linking a subject to an attribute or being present somewhere. The global existential être sense was inspected, with its impersonal examples. This absolute bank shares existence; before activation impact-review the family to broaden the impersonal wording transparently without resetting unchanged existential mastery or inventing an infinitive-only sense.')
new('éternel','éternel','adjective masculine singular','eternal; without beginning or end',['temporary','brief','recent'],'Dans cette conception, cet être n’a ni commencement ni fin : il est ___.',['éternel','temporaire','éphémère','récent'],'Quel adjectif qualifie ce qui n’a ni commencement ni fin ?',note='Éternel modifies the divine being within the giant’s conception. No proper French published or earlier eternal adjective family exists. The bank tests endless duration and does not assert the truth of a theology; all masculine singular alternatives fit the predicate.')
new('manifester','manifester','verb infinitive making evident','make evident; reveal',['hide','deny','forget'],'Rendre sa puissance visible, c’est ___ cette puissance.',['manifester','cacher','nier','oublier'],'Quel infinitif signifie rendre une qualité perceptible ou évidente ?',note='Manifester makes divine skill and power evident through creatures; it is not taking part in a political demonstration. No published or earlier French manifester family exists. The four infinitives fit the direct object cette puissance, while making evident contrasts with hiding, denying and forgetting.')
new('adresse','adresse','noun feminine singular skill','skill; ingenuity',['clumsiness','chance','strength'],'Cette réussite révèle une habileté inventive, plutôt que la force ou le hasard : elle révèle une grande ___.',['adresse','maladresse','chance','force'],'Quel nom féminin désigne l’habileté à réussir ce que l’on entreprend ?','prior:chapter-05-identity-plan.json:adresse_chapter_05_04_adresse',note='The Creator’s adresse is inventive skill, not a postal location or solely manual microscope dexterity. The earlier V skill plan and its three banks were inspected; this bank augments that same planned noun sense for the theological figure. Adresse/maladresse/chance/force are feminine singular; habileté selects adresse without a creative-only duplicate sense.')
new('puissance','puissance','noun feminine singular active power','power; effective ability to act',['weakness','chance','patience'],'La force qui permet d’agir et de produire ces effets est la ___.',['puissance','faiblesse','chance','patience'],'Quel nom féminin désigne ici la force ou le pouvoir d’agir ?','sns_zola_puissance_power',[(169,95),(208,13)],'Both source uses attribute effective creative power to the eternal being. The existing noun power family and its three political-power banks were read; the general force meaning applies, with these new contextual questions rather than an institution-only bank. All four nouns are feminine singular after la. The later potentiality use receives a distinct proposed meaning under the same noun lemma.')
new('puissance','puissance','noun feminine singular potential capacity','potentiality; capacity to be',['actual presence','appearance','memory'],'Ce qui rend possible une existence sans signifier sa réalisation actuelle est une ___.',['puissance','présence','apparence','mémoire'],'Quel nom féminin désigne une capacité possible, distincte de son actualisation ?','new:lem_zola_puissance',[(195,115)],'The Peripatetic defines a capacity of the soul to be what it is. This technical potentiality differs from the active power praised in units 169 and 208; prepare it on the existing proper French noun lemma. Puissance/présence/apparence/mémoire are feminine singular and fit une; potential capacity selects puissance. The text’s Aristotelian attribution is reported, not independently endorsed as an accurate quotation.')
new('goûter','goûter','verb infinitive figurative enjoyment','experience and enjoy',['fear','refuse','forget'],'Éprouver ces joies avec plaisir, c’est les ___.',['goûter','craindre','refuser','oublier'],'Quel infinitif signifie ici éprouver quelque chose avec plaisir ?',note='Goûter des joies figuratively means experiencing pleasure, not tasting food. No published or earlier proper French goûter family exists. Each infinitive fits les, and the pleasure clue selects goûter without requiring a physical taste sensation.')
new('joies','joie','noun feminine plural','joys; happy feelings',['sorrows','fears','shames'],'Les sentiments de bonheur qu’ils éprouvent sont leurs ___.',['joies','peines','craintes','hontes'],'Quel nom féminin pluriel désigne des sentiments de bonheur ?','sns_cendrillon_joie_sentiment_de_bonheur_de_satisfaction_vive_et_intense_qui_vient_du_plaisir_que_l_on_a_a_agir_a_accomplir_non_pas_une_tache_repetitive_mais_de_contribuer_a_un_certain_progres_qui_est_empreint_d_un_caractere_spirituel_philosophique_scientifique_religieux_ou_esthetique_9160942270',note='The giant assumes pure joys for the tiny people; the later reply challenges that assumption. The canonical French joie noun sense was compared with the older joy gloss; this is plural happy feeling, not a number-only meaning. Joies/peines/craintes/hontes are feminine plural and fit leurs; happiness alone selects joies.')
new('pures','pur','adjective feminine plural unmixed','pure; unmixed with something else',['mixed','clouded','bitter'],'Il imagine ces joies sans aucun mélange qui les altère : elles seraient ___.',['pures','mêlées','troubles','amères'],'Quel adjectif féminin pluriel signifie sans mélange ni altération ?','sns_loup_agneau_pur_qui_n_est_ni_souille_ni_melange_ici_en_parlant_de_l_eau_58fdd88fd2',note='Pures describes the speaker’s imagined unmixed joys, not literal clean water or a proved moral innocence. The existing adjective definition includes unsoiled/unmixed but specifies water. Record an explicit shared-family impact dependency to broaden contextual wording before activation, preserving unchanged purity mastery rather than inventing an abstract-only duplicate; all choices match feminine plural joies.')
new('paraissant','paraître','present participle seeming','seeming; appearing to be',['becoming','remaining','disappearing'],'___ n’être faits que d’esprit, ils donnent cette impression sans qu’elle soit démontrée.',['paraissant','croyant','prétendant','affirmant'],'Quel participe présent signifie donnant l’impression d’être ?','sns_fr_paraitre_seem',note='Paraissant tout esprit describes an appearance inferred from little matter. The global seem and appear families were inspected; preserve the previously chosen proper seem sense. Each participle takes the infinitive n’être; seeming differs from believing, claiming or affirming. No truth of an immaterial nature is asserted.')
new('esprit','esprit','noun masculine singular immaterial being','spirit; an immaterial being',['body','organ','muscle'],'Dans cette théorie, l’être pensant immatériel, opposé au corps, est un ___.',['esprit','corps','organe','muscle'],'Quel nom masculin désigne un être immatériel dans cette conception ?','sns_zola_esprit_supernatural',[(199,53),(200,23)],'The Cartesian’s âme est un esprit pur and the giant’s question about esprit concern an immaterial thinking entity. The global esprit family includes immaterial beings independently of group ethos and intellectual faculty. Add this philosophical context to the existing immaterial-being meaning, not a ghost-only interpretation or a philosopher-only duplicate. Esprit/corps/organe/muscle are masculine singular and fit un.')
new('esprits','esprit','noun masculine plural immaterial beings','spirits; immaterial beings',['bodies','organs','muscles'],'Dans cette conception, les êtres immatériels opposés aux corps sont des ___.',['esprits','corps','organes','muscles'],'Quel nom masculin pluriel désigne ici des êtres immatériels ?','sns_zola_esprit_supernatural',note='The giant likens the tiny people’s life to that of immaterial spirits. Existing plural questions invoke folklore, so this source-specific philosophical bank augments the same global immaterial-being sense. All four choices are masculine plural. The literal mind uses and group ethos are excluded, and no plural-only sense or new mastery copied from singular is invented.')
new('tous','tout','pronoun masculine plural group totality','all of them; every member',['several of them','some of them','a few of them'],'Sans aucune exception, les membres du groupe répondent : ils répondent ___.',['tous','plusieurs','certains','quelques-uns'],'Quel pronom masculin pluriel reprend la totalité d’un groupe, sans exception ?','sns_fr_toutes_all_of_them',[(182,205),(188,16),(189,30),(193,26),(193,76)],'All five standalone tous uses resume an entire plural group. The proper lem_fr_tout_pronoun owns the published all-of-them sense, currently worded for feminine toutes; broaden that gender-specific wording only after shared-family impact review. Do not attach the pronoun to a determiner lemma or invent a masculine-only sense. The four plural pronouns are grammatical, with no exception selecting tous.')
new('secouèrent','secouer','verb past historic plural shaking','shook; moved repeatedly back and forth',['lowered','turned away','covered'],'Ils firent bouger leur tête de côté et d’autre : ils la ___.',['secouèrent','baissèrent','détournèrent','couvrirent'],'Quel verbe au passé simple pluriel signifie firent bouger à plusieurs reprises ?',note='The philosophers shake their heads in response to the claim of happiness. The following admission supports dissent, but the lexical verb denotes shaking rather than a gesture-only sense. No published or earlier secouer family exists; the anatomical tête keeps its already planned noun meaning and no separate idiom is invented.')
new('franc','franc','adjective masculine singular honest','frank; sincere and open',['deceitful','reserved','insincere'],'Il exprime honnêtement ce qu’il pense, sans le dissimuler : il est ___.',['franc','trompeur','réservé','insincère'],'Quel adjectif qualifie une personne qui dit sincèrement ce qu’elle pense ?','new:lem_parure_franc_adjective_23d8fc24b6',note='Plus franc characterizes the philosopher’s open admission. The global franc adjective lemma has a freedom/Frankish gloss, while a separate noun lemma denotes currency; neither owns this honest meaning. Prepare sincerity under the proper existing French adjective lemma, preserving those other meanings. Each masculine singular predicate fits il est; candid expression selects franc.')
new('avoua','avouer','verb past historic singular admission','admitted; acknowledged openly',['denied','concealed','forgot'],'Il reconnut ouvertement cette triste réalité : il ___ ce fait.',['avoua','nia','cacha','oublia'],'Quel verbe au passé simple signifie reconnut ouvertement un fait ?','sns_zola_avouer_admit',note='The frank philosopher openly acknowledges the poor state of humanity. The global avouer admit sense already covers acknowledging what one might conceal; no confession of a personal crime is inferred. Add the past-historic surface and all three contextual bands to that same verb sense without a tense-only duplicate.')
new('excepte','excepter','verb present singular exclusion','excludes; leaves out',['includes','counts','describes'],'Pour laisser ce petit groupe hors du jugement général, on ___ ce petit groupe.',['excepte','inclut','compte','décrit'],'Quel verbe signifie laisse de côté comme une exception ?',note='The conditional excludes a small number of inhabitants from the unfavorable judgment about the rest. No global or earlier excepter family exists. All four third-person predicates fit the direct object ce petit groupe; exclusion rather than inclusion, counting or description selects excepte. The people are not literally expelled from a place.')
new('petit','petit','adjective masculine singular small quantity','small; few in quantity',['large','complete','unlimited'],'Ce nombre ne comprend que peu de personnes : il est ___.',['petit','grand','complet','illimité'],'Quel adjectif qualifie un nombre qui représente une faible quantité ?','sns_zola_petit_small',[(171,145),(185,23)],'Both petit nombre phrases describe a few inhabitants or sages, not their physical stature. The global small/young adjective family was read; before activation impact-review its scope wording to include numerical smallness. Retain unchanged smallness mastery and avoid a quantity-only duplicate. All four masculine singular adjectives fit nombre, with few in quantity selecting petit.')
new('considérés','considérer','past participle masculine plural social esteem','esteemed; regarded with respect',['despised','ignored','abandoned'],'On leur accorde de l’estime et du respect : ils sont ___.',['considérés','méprisés','ignorés','délaissés'],'Quel participe masculin pluriel signifie tenus en estime ?','new:lem_cendrillon_considerer_verb_7b6c9f7c8e',note='Fort peu considérés means little esteemed, not merely seldom observed visually. The global considérer verb family has attentive looking and mental examination but lacks social regard. Prepare esteem under that proper existing French verb lemma; the source’s low degree is carried by peu/fort rather than reversing the lexical meaning. All four participles match masculine plural inhabitants.')

